        "title": "Apple wins early access to OpenAI documents and employee testimony in trade secrets lawsuit",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/13/apple-wins-early-access-to-openai-documents-and-employee-testimony-in-trade-secrets-lawsuit/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/apple-openai.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Judge Edward Davila today granted some of Apple’s requests for expedited discovery in its trade secrets lawsuit against former employees, OpenAI, and io Products. Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"aapl,openai\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1074122\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/13/apple-wins-early-access-to-openai-documents-and-employee-testimony-in-trade-secrets-lawsuit/#more-1074122\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
